    "observations": [
      "World admission, upload requirements and draws now use ordered descriptors consistently; empty descriptor lists cannot resurrect legacy board/companion world draws. Explicit empty-layout background underlay remains.",
      "Main composed painter order remains panel, surface grids, ordered world bundles, schematic interaction and remaining original suffix. Removed branches only previously applied to empty descriptor lists.",
      "Schematic admission now depends on descriptor presence, not nonempty quad storage; this correctly allows stroke-only schematic payloads.",
      "Absent schematic source now requires no active GPU buffers for source match; upload preparation clears previous buffers when descriptors disappear. Existing tracked submissions retain retiring resources independently.",
      "Fixed world camera uniforms and schematic underlay buffer were removed from construction, recovery, upload and submission-reference paths together; descriptor-owned pane uniforms/grid storage remain.",
      "Resource stream count changes remove one obsolete physical stream, not logical consumers. Removed duplicated schematic CPU grid construction cannot alter composed grid output, which is still produced from descriptors.",
      "Source export fencing and test updates are consistent with owner-controlled keys."
    ],
